-- title:
--   Proof of Theorem 5.1, p. 446 — if X₁ ⪯icx X₂, there are X̂ᵢ ∼ Xᵢ on Ω with X̂₁ ≤ 𝔼[X̂₂ | X̂₁] a.s.
-- statement:
--   Let $(\Omega,\mathcal F,P)$ be a probability space on which a uniform random variable exists, $p\in[1,\infty)$, and $X_1,X_2\in\mathcal L_p(\Omega,\mathcal F,P)$ with $X_1\preceq_{\mathrm{icx}}X_2$. Then there are random variables $\widehat X_1,\widehat X_2\in\mathcal L_p(\Omega,\mathcal F,P)$ on the same space $\Omega$ with $\widehat X_1\overset{D}{\sim}X_1$, $\widehat X_2\overset{D}{\sim}X_2$ and
--
--   $$\widehat X_1\ \le\ \mathbb E\big[\widehat X_2\mid\widehat X_1\big]\qquad\text{a.s.}$$
--
--   The paper takes this from Müller and Stoyan (Corollary 1.5.21), see also Blackwell and Strassen. In the proof of Theorem 5.1 it is applied on the given space, so that the risk function can be evaluated at $\widehat X_1$, $\widehat X_2$ and $\mathbb E[\widehat X_2\mid\widehat X_1]$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\widehat X_1\overset{D}{\sim}X_1$ is equality of cdfs. $\mathbb E[\widehat X_2\mid\widehat X_1]$ is the conditional expectation given $\sigma(\widehat X_1)$, the $\sigma$-algebra generated by $\widehat X_1$; both $\widehat X_i$ are required to be measurable, so that $\sigma(\widehat X_1)\subset\mathcal F$. The coupling must live on $\Omega$ itself, which is why the existence of a uniform random variable is assumed.
-- source:
--   Ruszczyński, Shapiro, Optimization of convex risk functions, Math. Oper. Res. 31 (2006), p. 446, proof of Theorem 5.1, third paragraph (Müller and Stoyan [15, Corollary 1.5.21])

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_StochasticOrders_MonotoneConvex_IcxOrder
import Definitions.Def_ConvexRiskFn_Order_Setting
open MeasureTheory

namespace ConvexRiskFn.Order

/-- Proof of Theorem 5.1, p. 446 (Müller and Stoyan, Corollary 1.5.21; Blackwell; Strassen): if
`X₁ ⪯_icx X₂` in `ℒ_p(Ω, ℱ, P)` and `(Ω, ℱ, P)` carries a uniform random variable, there are
random variables `X̂₁ ∼ X₁`, `X̂₂ ∼ X₂` on the same `Ω` with `X̂₁ ≤ 𝔼[X̂₂ | X̂₁]` a.s. -/
theorem strassen_icx_coupling {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (P : Measure Ω)
    [IsProbabilityMeasure P] (p : ENNReal) (hp1 : 1 ≤ p) (hpt : p ≠ ⊤)
    (hU : ∃ U : Ω → ℝ, IsUniformRV P U) (X₁ X₂ : Ω → ℝ) (h₁ : MemLp X₁ p P) (h₂ : MemLp X₂ p P)
    (h : StochasticOrders.MonotoneConvex.IcxOrder P P X₁ X₂) :
    ∃ Xh₁ Xh₂ : Ω → ℝ, Measurable Xh₁ ∧ Measurable Xh₂ ∧ MemLp Xh₁ p P ∧ MemLp Xh₂ p P ∧
      (∀ t : ℝ, P {ω | Xh₁ ω ≤ t} = P {ω | X₁ ω ≤ t}) ∧
      (∀ t : ℝ, P {ω | Xh₂ ω ≤ t} = P {ω | X₂ ω ≤ t}) ∧
      Xh₁ ≤ᵐ[P] P[Xh₂|MeasurableSpace.comap Xh₁ inferInstance] := by sorry

end ConvexRiskFn.Order
